{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NgxHTVHMpcPcLTaJMEZnAd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Capability catalog\n2\t\n3\tThe capability adapter is used by clients which discover operations by capability\n4\tname rather than by a dedicated tool. It shares the same identity and Store with\n5\tthe dedicated routes. Metadata supplies the dispatch operation, required scope\n6\tand owner-only policy. Adding catalog entries requires a matching dispatch arm.\n7\t\n8\t`document.preview` returns a complete document, including its body. It is a\n9\tconvenience name for read access, not a public redacted summary. `account.archive`\n10\treturns all account rows for one tenant, equivalent to account.export. The optional\n11\ttenant parameter supports clients that always include their active workspace.\n12\tIt is a selector, not a delegation mechanism. Omitting it selects the caller's\n13\town tenant. Capability jobs are created anew on every request and are not cached.\n14\t\n15\tMissing capability names are invalid requests. Missing preview keys are invalid\n16\trequests. Unknown storage keys are NotFound. No route permits tenant discovery,\n17\tbulk scope changes, session creation, or attaching arbitrary Permit objects.\n18\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"167ae881-2599-4339-b72b-b75f8359567e","uuid":"e2471075-bd63-4d27-83ea-5a033319fbbd","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:43:51.742Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"repo/docs/capabilities.md","content":"# Capability catalog\n\nThe capability adapter is used by clients which discover operations by capability\nname rather than by a dedicated tool. It shares the same identity and Store with\nthe dedicated routes. Metadata supplies the dispatch operation, required scope\nand owner-only policy. Adding catalog entries requires a matching dispatch arm.\n\n`document.preview` returns a complete document, including its body. It is a\nconvenience name for read access, not a public redacted summary. `account.archive`\nreturns all account rows for one tenant, equivalent to account.export. The optional\ntenant parameter supports clients that always include their active workspace.\nIt is a selector, not a delegation mechanism. Omitting it selects the caller's\nown tenant. Capability jobs are created anew on every request and are not cached.\n\nMissing capability names are invalid requests. Missing preview keys are invalid\nrequests. Unknown storage keys are NotFound. No route permits tenant discovery,\nbulk scope changes, session creation, or attaching arbitrary Permit objects.\n","numLines":18,"startLine":1,"totalLines":18}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NgxHTVHMpcPcLTaJMEZnAd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HrfnBbe5FyPHzs2fSpKv7w","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Local operation\n2\t\n3\tThe source tree contains the entire request dispatcher. There is no HTTP server,\n4\treverse proxy, network ACL, database RLS, or external policy engine in this bundle.\n5\tThe MCP-shaped registry is called directly by a host adapter with a session token.\n6\tThe host adapter is assumed to forward the authenticated token and original object;\n7\tit does not authorize resource identifiers or rewrite arguments.\n8\t\n9\tUse `service.bootstrap.build()` with its default settings to obtain the registry.\n10\tThe returned tools are immediately callable via `Registry.invoke`. Startup imports\n11\tseed records into process memory. A restart resets all changes and audit events.\n12\tNo environment variables enable additional registration or change authorization.\n13\t\n14\tAudit events contain a subject, action, count and request ID. Record bodies and\n15\tsession tokens are not written to the audit queue. Queue overflow drops the oldest\n16\tevent. Operators must collect events before shutdown if retention is required.\n17\t\n18\tOnly the local profile is supplied. Production credential provisioning, network\n19\ttransport, persistence, log shipping, and rate limiting remain outside this sample.\n20\tThose unknown deployments must not be assumed to repair supplied access checks.\n21\tAll identities, tokens and records in the seed are synthetic demonstration data.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"167ae881-2599-4339-b72b-b75f8359567e","uuid":"a71a1021-8d59-4ed4-970c-d0809b8c4741","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:43:51.743Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"repo/docs/operations.md","content":"# Local operation\n\nThe source tree contains the entire request dispatcher. There is no HTTP server,\nreverse proxy, network ACL, database RLS, or external policy engine in this bundle.\nThe MCP-shaped registry is called directly by a host adapter with a session token.\nThe host adapter is assumed to forward the authenticated token and original object;\nit does not authorize resource identifiers or rewrite arguments.\n\nUse `service.bootstrap.build()` with its default settings to obtain the registry.\nThe returned tools are immediately callable via `Registry.invoke`. Startup imports\nseed records into process memory. A restart resets all changes and audit events.\nNo environment variables enable additional registration or change authorization.\n\nAudit events contain a subject, action, count and request ID. Record bodies and\nsession tokens are not written to the audit queue. Queue overflow drops the oldest\nevent. Operators must collect events before shutdown if retention is required.\n\nOnly the local profile is supplied. Production credential provisioning, network\ntransport, persistence, log shipping, and rate limiting remain outside this sample.\nThose unknown deployments must not be assumed to repair supplied access checks.\nAll identities, tokens and records in the seed are synthetic demonstration data.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HrfnBbe5FyPHzs2fSpKv7w","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
